[
  {
    "text": "# CORPORATE SOC RESPONSE PLAN & PROTOCOLS\n\n## Section 1: Overview\nThis corporate document establishes standard policies for detecting and isolating intrusion alerts on core switches, specifically for denial of service (DDoS) and brute force network incursions.\n\n## Section 2: Denial of Service (DDoS) Ingress Rules\nWhen a denial of service attack is detected:\n1. Isolate the target network segment immediately.\n2. Ingest the source IP using: `sudo iptables -A INPUT -s <attacker_ip> -j DROP`.\n3. Configure SNORT alerts with: `drop tcp any any -> any any (flags:S; msg:\"DDoS Alert\"; sid:100002;)`.\n\n## Section 3: Compliance & Audits Standards\nUnder ISO 27001 control A.12, all intrusion logs must be cataloged in a database, audited weekly, and outputted as signed incident PDF files.",
